	(text "Core board per spec §2a, §4, §5, §6. MCU pads per the §5 table (E12); MDBT50Q-U1MV2 second source assumed pad-identical (unverified).\nPack OR: J_BAT_A/B (1 PACK+, 2 GND, 3 GND, 4 PACK+) -> LM66200 U402 -> VBAT. Each pack input <= 1 uF (E14: hot-swap window scales with it).\nUVLO: TPS3840PH18 on BAT54C-OR'd packs drives ~ON high below ~1.9 V. SW403 (slide) picks ~ON: supervisor (on) or SUP_VDD (packs off, 0 uA); R403 10M holds 'on' in the gap.\nVBUS_IN = LM66200 U404 OR of VBUS_LOCAL (J_USB) and VBUS_LINK_IN (J_LINK). VSYS = TPS2116 U408: IN1 TLV75733P from VBUS_IN, IN2 logic boost from VBAT;\nPR1 301k/100k from VBUS_IN (drops to IN2 at 3.63-4.40 V). Logic boost variants: 'tps61099' U406 576k/249k (default) or 'max17222' U407 RSEL 80.6k via R426 0 ohm.\nLED rail = TPS2116 U410: IN1 VBUS_IN, IN2 TPS61023 U409 (698k/100k -> 4.75 V, EN pulled up to VSYS); PR1 301k/100k, 1M PR1-ST hysteresis (E3).\nExpansion 3V3: TLV75733P U411 from LED_RAIL, EN from GPIO with 100k pull-down, 150 mA budget. Pull-ups to EXP_3V3: keep MCU pins low or undriven while it is off.\nVBAT sense: Q401 AO3415A switches 49.9k/49.9k from VBAT when BAT_DIV_EN (also the module-ID pull-up top) is high; R440 1M holds it off while undriven; AIN0 <= 1.9 V. CC1/CC2 100k into AINx.\nJ_LED 1 RAIL 2 GND 3 SDA 4 VSYS 5 SDB 6 GND | 7 GND 8 ID 9 VSYS 10 SCL 11 GND 12 RAIL. J_ROW 1-3 ROW0-2, 4 GND, 5-7 ROW3-5.\nJ_COL 1 GND, 2-10 COL0-8, 11 ENC_A, 12 ENC_B, 13 GND. J_LINK 1 VBUS_LINK_IN 2 GND 3 U0_TX 4 U1_A 5 GND 6 LINK_SW_EN 7 VBUS_IN_OUT | mirrored to 14.\nAll key-board headers reversal-safe (pin k meets N+1-k). Li-ion reservation (spec §15): JP401 bridged VDDH-VDD, C406 and L401 (REG0) not fitted. J401 TC2030-NL footprint only."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
